        "original_id": "7ad45c3b-62f9-5c66-865b-4e67ec905f81",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Tom Courtenay, John Mills, Robert Emmet Smith\n- Films: King Rat, The Loneliness of the Long Distance Runner, Billy Liar, Doctor Zhivago\n- Awards and Honors: Academy Award for Best Art Direction, knighthood\n\nFacts:\n- Tom Courtenay was born on 25 February 1937 and is an English actor.\n- Tom Courtenay came to prominence in the early 1960s with the films The Loneliness of the Long Distance Runner (1962), Billy Liar (1963), and Doctor Zhivago (1965).\n- John Mills and Tom Courtenay were among the supporting cast of the film King Rat.\n- Robert Emmet Smith was nominated for an Academy Award for Best Art Direction for the film King Rat.\n- Tom Courtenay received a knighthood in February 2001 for services to cinema and theatre.",
